hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1563","On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Abu Ahmad, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib. H. Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, and this is a hadith. Bundar, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we liked to be on his right, so I heard him say when he left: “My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.” He did not say hello when he left"
"1564","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Bara’, on the authority of his father, he said: “ “It pleased us to pray from the one next to the right of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because he used to begin with the salutation on his right.”"
"1565","Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, Abu Ahmad informed us, Mus’ar informed us, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ibn al-Baraa, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Azib He said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we liked to be at his right. And I heard him say when he left: “My Lord, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants.”"
